---
// Terms of service. Written to match what the rest of the site already
// promises — /for-practices/, /advertise/, /how-we-rank/ and
// /ownership-disclosure/ — rather than generic boilerplate. If you change a
// commitment on one of those pages, change it here too; terms that contradict
// the marketing page are worse than no terms at all.
//
// NOT REVIEWED BY COUNSEL as of 2026-09-18. This is an honest, plain-language
// description of how the business actually operates, which is the right
// starting point, but have a lawyer read it before it carries real weight —
// particularly the liability, refund and governing-law sections.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { breadcrumbLd } from '../lib/schema.js';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site.js';

const crumbs = [{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Terms', href: '/terms/' }];
const updated = '2026-09-18';
const sp = SITE.pricing.sponsor;
---
<Base title="Terms of service"
      description="The terms that apply to using PainBeacon, claiming a practice listing, buying a paid listing, and sponsoring pages."
      jsonld={breadcrumbLd(crumbs)}>
  <div class="wrap narrow prose">
    <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
    <h1>Terms of service</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Plain language, and only what is actually true of how we operate. Last updated {updated}.
      These terms cover everyone: people reading the directory, practices claiming or buying a
      listing, and businesses sponsoring pages.
    </p>

    <h2>Who we are, and what this is not</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE.name} is an independent directory and information service run by {SITE.legalName}.
      We are <strong>not a medical provider</strong>, we do not deliver care, and nothing on
      this site is medical advice. Listings are not endorsements or referrals. Choosing a
      clinician is your decision, made with a clinician — never on the strength of a directory
      entry alone. If you have a medical emergency, call 911.
    </p>

    <h2>The directory itself</h2>
    <p>
      Clinic records are built from public sources, principally the federal NPI registry, and
      from information practices give us. Public data goes stale: an address, a phone number,
      or a set of hours may be wrong, and a clinician may have moved or retired. We correct what
      we learn about, and we invite corrections at
      <a href={`mailto:contactus@${SITE.url.replace('https://', '')}`}>contactus@painbeacon.com</a>,
      but we cannot promise any record is current or complete. Verify anything that matters
      directly with the practice.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Every practice is listed for free and always will be.</strong> No practice pays to
      appear in the directory, and no practice can pay to be removed from it in order to hide a
      record that is accurate.
    </p>

    <h2>Rankings are never for sale</h2>
    <p>
      This is the one that matters most, so it is a term and not just a marketing line. We rank
      clinics on objective, published criteria, set out in full at
      <a href="/how-we-rank/">how we rank</a>. <strong>No payment of any kind — a paid listing,
      a sponsorship, or anything else — changes a clinic's rank, its position in any list, or
      what we write.</strong> Paid placements are labeled and sit outside ranked lists. If we
      ever become affiliated with a listed clinic, that is disclosed on the listing and at
      <a href="/ownership-disclosure/">ownership disclosure</a>, and the criteria do not bend
      to favor it.
    </p>

    <h2>Claiming a practice</h2>
    <p>
      Claiming and verification are free. When you claim a listing you are telling us you are
      authorized to act for that practice, and we confirm that before any change goes live. We
      may ask for evidence, and we may decline or reverse a claim we cannot verify. You are
      responsible for what you submit being accurate and for having the right to use it.
    </p>

    <h2>Paid listings</h2>
    <p>
      Enhanced and Featured are described at <a href="/for-practices/">for practices</a>, and
      the price shown there is the price charged. Specifically:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Verification comes first.</strong> We verify you represent the practice before an
        upgraded listing goes live. If we cannot verify it, we refund you in full.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Monthly plans</strong> renew automatically until you cancel. Cancel any time and
        it runs to the end of the period you have paid for. We do not refund part-months.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Prepaid terms</strong> bill three months and run four, starting the day the
        listing goes live rather than the day you pay, and renew month to month afterward at
        the then-current price. The fourth month is a launch offer: we can withdraw it at any
        time, and if we do, it never shortens a term already bought. Whatever the page said on
        the day you paid is what you get.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Featured is one practice per area.</strong> Where an area is already taken, it is
        not available at any price until it opens up. Availability is not guaranteed and is not
        reserved by payment alone.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>What a paid listing buys is presentation, not performance.</strong> More room,
        better placement outside the rankings, and a badge. We do not promise traffic, calls,
        bookings, patients, or a ranking position, and none of those is a condition of the fee.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Sponsorships</h2>
    <p>
      Businesses that are not clinics can sponsor pages by state; the rates and rules are at
      <a href="/advertise/">advertise</a>. Sponsorship terms are {sp.term.toLowerCase()}, or prepaid by the
      quarter. Each sponsor gets category exclusivity in the states it buys,
      for the term it has paid for. Cards are labeled “Advertisement,” carry the line that
      sponsors never influence rankings or editorial, and sit outside every ranked list.
    </p>
    <p>
      Creative is subject to our approval, and we decline copy that makes a medical claim.
      Advertising must comply with the rules of the states it appears in — attorney advertising
      and health advertising in particular — and that compliance is the sponsor's
      responsibility, not ours. We may pause or remove creative that puts us or a reader at risk.
    </p>

    <h2>Content you give us</h2>
    <p>
      You keep ownership of what you submit. You give us permission to display, resize and
      distribute it as part of the directory and its syndicated feeds, for as long as your
      listing runs and for a reasonable period afterward in archives and caches we do not
      control. You confirm you have the right to give us that permission. We may decline or
      remove anything that is inaccurate, misleading, unlawful, makes a medical claim, or
      would breach a professional advertising rule.
    </p>

    <h2>Payment</h2>
    <p>
      Card payments are processed by Stripe under their terms; we never see or store card
      numbers. Sponsorships and some listings are invoiced instead. Prices can change with
      notice on the relevant page, and a change never affects a prepaid term already running.
      You are responsible for any taxes that apply to your purchase where we are not required
      to collect them.
    </p>

    <h2>Ending it</h2>
    <p>
      You can cancel at any time, as described above. We can decline, pause, or end a paid
      listing or sponsorship — for a breach of these terms, a failed verification, or creative
      we will not run. If we end a paid arrangement for any reason other than your breach, we
      refund the unused portion of what you prepaid. Removing a paid upgrade does not remove
      the free listing, which stays as an ordinary directory record.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranty, and what we are liable for</h2>
    <p>
      The site is provided as is. We do not warrant that it will be uninterrupted, error-free,
      or that any information in it is accurate or current. To the fullest extent the law
      allows, {SITE.legalName} is not liable for indirect, incidental, or consequential
      damages, or for lost profits, revenue, patients or goodwill. Where we are liable, our
      total liability is limited to what you paid us in the twelve months before the claim.
      Nothing here limits liability that cannot be limited by law.
    </p>

    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      How we handle information is set out at <a href="/privacy/">privacy</a>, which is part of
      these terms. The short version: the site runs no tracking scripts and sets no advertising
      cookies, and we intend to keep it that way.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes, law, and reaching us</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms; the date at the top changes when we do, and a material change
      to a paid arrangement will not apply to a term you have already prepaid. These terms are
      governed by the laws of the Commonwealth of Virginia, without regard to its conflict of
      laws rules, and any dispute belongs in the state or federal courts located in Virginia.
    </p>
    <p>
      Questions, corrections, or a complaint about anything above:
      <a href={`mailto:contactus@${SITE.url.replace('https://', '')}`}>contactus@painbeacon.com</a>.
      We read everything that arrives there.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
